+## C1 — Delay classification (PROVEN)
+
+For `ẋ = −αx(t) − βx(t−τ)`: `|β| < α` ⟺ delay-independent stability; `|β| > α, α+β > 0` ⟺ stable iff `τ < τ* = arccos(−α/β)/√(β²−α²)`. Every imaginary-axis crossing is rightward.
+
+## C2 — Substitution (linear PROVEN; nonlinear target stated)
+
+Linear domain: Farkas is the exact classification. Nonlinear: MFCQ + Clarke alternative (conjectural bridge).
+
+## C3 — Aggregation closure (PROVED)
+
+Exact closure ⟺ dPF fibre-constant (projectability). Non-atomic: no finite raw-moment family closes. Finite/atomic: closures exist (two-atom case verified). Approximate: P-saturation/lift-typed erosion.
+
+## C4 — Diagnostic classification (PROVED)
+
+Separation ⟺ soundness; uniform-horizon theorem (compact certified sets exit within finite N); rate structure is the strictly finer adversarial-exit subclass.
+
+## C5 — Bifurcation (PARTIAL)
+
+Both extremal witnesses proved. Transversality classification theorem stated, not proved.
+
+## C6 — Information/implementation (PROVED)
+
+Refinement monotone iff typed-lift hypotheses; implementation enlargement never monotone (all-branches); delayed-revelation inert iff obstruction unreached.
